  "body": "Opening a malformed or semantically invalid project now keeps the existing document, history and filename on both disk and picked-byte paths. Each loader builds a replacement world first; only a successful load retires the old document. Successful opens preserve the user's theme and colour-vision preferences, and disk failures name the attempted file.\n\nValidation:\n- `refused_disk_project_keeps_document_and_history`\n- `refused_byte_project_keeps_document_and_history`\n- Each regression test covers malformed JSON and a semantic failure after loader writes begin, checking serialized content, undo/redo, dirty state, filename/title and document version.\n- Both tests fail with the original implementations restored using `cp`, and pass with the fix restored.\n- All 10 `file_pick_tests` pass, including successful disk replacement and preference preservation.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`\n\nReadings: project load/apply implementation, disk and byte open handlers, UI steering, and work-issue skill. Decision recorded in `docs/decisions/1613-open-keeps-document.md`.\n\nBase: current upstream/main, as requested; fork main was not changed. Effort: medium. Configured Sonnet worker model unavailable in this session; used session Codex model.\n\nNot exercised: interactive desktop/browser file pickers. `graphify update` unavailable because graphify is not installed.\n\nChangelog: Failed project opens preserve the current document, history and filename.\n\nFixes #1613\n",
